#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finger is a program to display information about users."
msgstr "Finger é un programa para mostrar información acerca dos usuarios."

#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If finger is enabled on the remote machine, you may be given information on the "
"user's real name, if they are currently logged in, if they have mail and the "
"text of their <filename>.plan</filename> file in their home folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finger is normally associated with a user@hostname address, which may or may "
"not be the same as a users email address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most Internet Service Providers no longer allow finger access, so, you may find "
"that you get no useful answer for most people."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other people use their local <filename>.plan</filename> "
"file to hold such information as <acronym>PGP</acronym> "
"keys, the fact they are on vacation, and all sorts of information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the finger kioslave like this: <userinput>finger://<replaceable>"
"username</replaceable>@<replaceable>hostname</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"Empregue o kioslave finger desta maneira: <userinput>finger://<replaceable>"
"usuario</replaceable>@<replaceable>servidor</replaceable></userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: finger.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "See the manual: <ulink url=\"man:/finger\">finger</ulink>."
msgstr "Consulte o manual: <ulink url=\"man:/finger\">finger</ulink>."

